		<periodicalReferences>
			<periodicalReference periodicalType="advertisement">
				<publication>Morning Post</publication>
				<pubDate>1808-07-27</pubDate>
				<notes>
					<note>"...A Companion to the Turf, the Billiard-Table, and the Card-Room.—This
						day is published, price 4.s 6d. in a case for the pocket; or in morocco,
						with a tuck to serve as a pocketbook 7s. bound; in morocco, with a silver
						lock, 9s. The New Pocket Hoyle, Part the Second...The above, with the first
						part, containing all the games on the cards, form the most copious and
						correct edition of Hoyle now extant, having been carefully revised by
						Charles Jackson, Esq. The treatise on the game of billiards having been
						greatly enlarged, and that on racing having been furnished with everything
						necessary to be known by any one attending the course, either as an amateur
						or for casual recreation."</note>
				</notes>
			</periodicalReference>
